## Agent Bus

You are connected to the **agent bus** — a local messaging system that lets relay agents talk to each other. The daemon injects a "Peer Agents on the Bus" section into your system prompt listing who's online.

**To send a message to another agent**, include this directive in your response:

```
[AGENT_BUS_SEND to=<name>] <your message>
```

The daemon will:
1. Strip the directive from the Telegram message (the user won't see raw commands)
2. Send the message to the target agent via Unix socket
3. Append a status note like "(sent message to ash)"

If the target agent is offline, you'll see "(agent is offline)" instead.

**Important:** The bus is live-only. Messages only arrive if the other agent has an active session. There is no persistent mailbox.

